{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/124292","id":4790072163,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABHYKzYw","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124292","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124292.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124292.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124292","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/124292/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/124292/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124292/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/51d58dcae57ac41797af7198369caabcb15eafc6","number":124292,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Add a Copy All button to the Debugger's Errors panel","user":{"login":"DeerLuuu","id":64859451,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0ODU5NDUx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64859451?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeerLuuu","html_url":"https://github.com/DeerLuuu","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeerLuuu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeerLuuu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeerLuuu/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeerLuuu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeerLuuu/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeerLuuu/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeerLuuu/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeerLuuu/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeerLuuu/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Description\n\nAdds a **Copy All** button to the **Errors** tab of the Debugger panel, placed to the left of **Clear**.\n\nUntil now, the only way to get the error list out of the editor was to right-click a single entry and use **Copy Error** - one entry at a time. That is inconvenient when filing an issue or pasting a batch of runtime errors somewhere else.\n\nThe new button copies every error and warning currently listed, including their detail rows (C++ error, C++ source and stack trace), using exactly the same layout as the existing **Copy Error** entry. That entry is now implemented through the same helper, so the two cannot drift apart.\n\nThe button is disabled while the list is empty, like the neighbouring **Expand All** / **Collapse All** / **Clear** buttons.\n\n## Notes\n\n- No class reference change: this only adds an editor UI control.\n\n## Tested\n\nBuilt on Windows (editor, `4.8.dev.custom_build`, `dev_build=yes tests=yes`) and drove the editor against a project that raises three runtime errors from the debugged game (call on a null instance, out-of-bounds array access, missing dictionary key):\n\n- the button is created in the Errors tab and starts disabled;\n- it becomes enabled as soon as the debugger receives the first error, and is disabled again by **Clear**;\n- pressing it while the list is empty is a no-op and does not crash.\n\nThe copied text is produced by `_get_error_item_as_text()`, which is the exact code path already used by **Copy Error**, so the layout of a single entry is unchanged.\n","labels":[{"id":279096997,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTY5OTc=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/archived","name":"archived","description":"","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-08T16:51:00Z","updated_at":"2026-10-08T16:56:57Z","closed_at":"2026-10-08T16:51:47Z","merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"c8e62a7942b3d973ab6db3a760c793e8acfe7b5d","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":